stance_counts) AS NumberOfEvents\n            ```\n            \n            Always provide the Zenodo link `https://zenodo.org/records/14616124` of the docker container holding\n            the full Neo4j graph database where the user can access the complete result with the cypher query.\n            ", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "tool", "name": "CypherSearch", "id": "932f8d57-5884-466d-9599-43655af65eb8", "tool_call_id": "call_D7wdsG3HbsjQVbB8cGc81r1P", "artifact": null, "status": "success"}}, {"type": "ai", "data": {"content": "Here is a summary of how many substances typically contribute TU > 0.001 for Algae at sampling events (site-year-quarter) where the sum of toxic units (sumTU) for Algae exceeds 1:\n\n| Statistic                   | Value         |\n|-----------------------------|--------------|\n| Mean number of substances   | 13.78        |\n| Median number of substances | (not available) |\n| Minimum per event           | (see below)  |\n| Maximum per event           | (see below)  |\n| Number of events analyzed   | 221          |\n\n- The mean number of substances per event with TU > 0.001 is approximately 13.8.\n- The minimum and maximum values per event are available as lists, indicating a wide range, but the typical (median) value could not be determined from the data provided.\n\nTextual summary:\nAt events where the summed toxic impact for Algae is acutely toxic (sumTU > 1), on average about 14 substances per event contribute at a level (TU > 0.001) that may cause chronic impacts. This suggests that, in these high-risk events, the toxic pressure is typically distributed across a mixture of multiple substances.\n\nCypher query used:\n```\n// Step 1: Find all site-year-quarter events where sumTU for algae exceeds 1\nMATCH (site:Site)-[impact:SUMMARIZED_IMPACT_ON]->(species:Species)\nWHERE species.name = 'algae' AND impact.sumTU > 1\nWITH site, impact.year AS year, impact.quarter AS quarter\n\n// Step 2: For each event, count the number of substances with TU_algae > 0.001\nMATCH (sub:Substance)-[meas:MEASURED_AT]->(site)\nWHERE meas.year = year AND meas.quarter = quarter AND meas.TU_algae > 0.001\n\nWITH site.name AS SiteName, year, quarter, count(DISTINCT sub) AS n_substances\nORDER BY SiteName, year, quarter\n\n// Step 3: Summarize the typical number of such substances per event\nWITH collect(n_substances) AS substance_counts\nRETURN\n  apoc.agg.median(substance_counts) AS MedianSubstancesPerEvent,\n  avg(reduce(s = 0.0, x IN substance_counts | s + toFloat(x)) / toFloat(size(substance_counts))) AS MeanSubstancesPerEvent,\n  min(substance_counts) AS MinSubstancesPerEvent,\n  max(substance_counts) AS MaxSubstancesPerEvent,\n  size(substance_counts) AS NumberOfEvents\n```\n\nFor full access to the underlying data and further analysis, you can use the Neo4j graph database available at Zenodo: https://zenodo.org/records/14616124", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "stop", "model_name": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14", "system_fingerprint": "fp_515e001228", "service_tier": "default", "model_provider": "openai"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--01a1d9aa-ce2b-7406-807e-9c24c1fef7bd", "tool_calls": [], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 5307, "output_tokens": 580, "total_tokens": 5887, "input_token_details": {"audio": 0, "cache_read": 2688}, "output_token_details": {"audio": 0, "reasoning": 0}}}}]